UID:berkeley:20261015T220000Z-327522@events.berkeley.edu
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260925T042715Z
DTSTART:20261015T220000Z
DTEND:20261016T000000Z
SUMMARY:OSPO Monthly Meetup: Open source AI models
LOCATION:Gateway Building\, Social Kitchen\, Room 1420
DESCRIPTION:Join BIDS and D-Lab in shaping the future of open source at UC
  Berkeley\, building on its rich legacy of leadership in open source softw
 are development. There will be a fireside chat\, a Q&A session\, and commu
 nity gathering time with drinks and snacks! → Attend in person: Register
  on this page and join us at 3pm. → Attend online: Sign up here to recei
 ve a Zoom link (https://forms.gle/fKjzxbKFScfAMxks5) and join us at 3:30pm
 . The focus of this month's OSPO is on open source AI\, sovereign implemen
 tations\, data privacy\, researcher and user surveillance\, and creating a
  more diverse AI ecosystem. We are joined by Fernando Pérez\, BIDS Facult
 y Director and Project Jupyter Co-Founder. He is a co-author of a recent N
 ature commentary "Why scientists should lead the shift away from AI mega d
 ata centres" (https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02451-2). Join us
  to explore how we can harness the collective intelligence and creativity 
 of the global open source ecosystem to meaningfully transform how knowledg
 e is created and sharedCheck out the rest of the series (https://bids.berk
 eley.edu/programs-initiatives/open-source-program-office-ospo)!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.berkeley.edu/BIDS/event/327522-ospo-monthly-m
 eetup-open-source-ai-models
END:VEVENT
